## Summary
The article discusses plans to allocate annual tax revenues of approximately 1.5 trillion won from tobacco consumption and local education taxes towards funding public housing supply. This initiative aims to repurpose specific tax funds to support housing projects.

## Key Points
- Annual tax revenues from tobacco consumption and local education taxes total around 1.5 trillion won.
- These revenues are being directed to fund public housing supply projects.
- The policy represents a shift in the use of tax funds from other potential purposes.
- Public housing supply is explicitly designated as the use for these taxes.
- The measure involves both tobacco consumption tax and local education tax components.


